{"type":"message","id":"b5d7fd9f","parentId":"bebdfec4","timestamp":"2026-02-12T16:59:11.323Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I can see the serve command. To start the server, I'll use:\n`opencode serve --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096 --model opencode/kimi-k2.5`\n\nBut the serve command starts the server in the current directory. I need to cd to /root/.openclaw/workspace/claw-config first, or specify the project path. Let me check if serve accepts a project argument:\n\nLooking at the help: `opencode [project]` is the tui command. The `serve` command has options but no positional project argument. So I need to cd to the claw-config directory and then run `opencode serve --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096 --model opencode/kimi-k2.5`.\n\nBut I also need to attach a client. I can either:\n1. Start the server in background, then attach using `opencode attach <url>`\n2. Or start the server and wait for connection\n\nThe user said \"attach a client to begin working\" - I should start the server and then also attach a client to it. This could be done in a background process.\n\nLet me start the server as a background process, then attach to it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-45b4e7eca4e94c9c92c1d62d5dbdd202","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/.openclaw/workspace/claw-config && opencode serve --hostname 0.0.0.0 --port 4096 --model opencode/kimi-k2.5 &","background":true,"yieldMs":5000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":12633,"output":616,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13249,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770915547143}}
