{"type":"message","id":"95275c05","parentId":"c0c786ba","timestamp":"2026-02-12T17:00:58.590Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The logs are ansi escape codes, but I can parse the model line: \n```\n[15;14H[38;2;238;238;238m[48;2;30;30;30mKi[0m[15;18H[38;2;238;238;238m[48;2;30;30;30m K2.5[0m[15;23H[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;30;30;30m \n[0m[15;24H[38;2;128;128;128m[48;2;30;30;30mNvidia\n```\nIt shows \"Ki K2.5 Nvidia\" - that indicates the model is Kimi K2.5 from Nvidia provider. So the client is connected and the correct model is selected. Also the path shows \"~/.openclaw/workspace/claw-config\". So everything is set.\n\nNow the user wants to \"attach a client to begin working\". The client is attached and ready. I should report that the server is running and the client is attached, and ask what task they'd like to work on, or proactively offer to send tasks to OpenCode.\n\nBut I should also verify Build mode is active. In the UI, I see \"Build\" in the status line. That's good.\n\nI need to produce a clear summary: server URL, port, model, workspace directory, and that the client is attached. Then I should ask what they want to code, or perhaps I can offer to send a task.\n\nGiven the instructions: \"Be proactive: Once a server is running, offer to send tasks to OpenCode, monitor progress, and help interpret results. You can attach your own client to the same server to collaborate in real-time.\"\n\nI've already attached a client. I could also attach myself as a second client if needed, but I think as the assistant I can send tasks via the attach session using process write. However, OpenCode's attach is a TUI, not a direct API. To send tasks programmatically, I might need to use the `opencode run` command with a message, which will connect to the server and execute a task. That could be used to send tasks to the running server.\n\nAlternatively, I could instruct the user to interact with the TUI, but as an assistant I can also send tasks directly.\n\nI should confirm the server details and ask the user for their first task. Also, I should note that the server is on port 4097 (due to a conflict) but that's still LAN accessible. The user asked for 4096, but I can explain if needed.\n\nLet me craft a summary.\n\nOne more thing: I should ensure the server is indeed on the LAN. It's bound to 0.0.0.0, so accessible from other machines on the network at <host-ip>:4097. I should mention the IP if possible. I can find the IP address of the machine.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-670903fe8d244831bbac3435c003d224","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"hostname -I | awk '{print $1}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":32436,"output":1262,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33698,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770915650534}}
