{"type":"message","id":"f759bceb","parentId":"49a2e8d6","timestamp":"2026-02-12T17:01:23.294Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! Both PIDs (1845 and 1838) have cwd /root/.openclaw/workspace/claw-config. That means both servers are running from the correct directory. The one on 4096 is also from claw-config. So maybe when we started the first serve after killing the old mmit-checkin one, it succeeded on 4096. Then we started another one on 4097 mistakenly. So we have two servers from the same directory, which is redundant. I'll kill the server on 4096 to leave only the one on 4097, or I could kill the one on 4097 and keep 4096. But the user asked for 0.0.0.0:4096. Since we have a server on 4096 that is correctly set up, I could just keep that and kill the one on 4097. However, our attach session is connected to 4097. If we kill 4097, the attach will lose connection. But we can re-attach to 4096.\n\nLet's decide: The user explicitly said \"Start the server on 0.0.0.0:4096\". I should aim to have the server on 4096. The current server on 4096 is from claw-config and is running. So I should kill the server on 4097, and re-attach the client to 4096.\n\nLet's kill the server on 4097 (PID 1968 and maybe its wrapper 1959).","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Both servers are from the claw-config directory. I'll consolidate to just the one on port 4096 as requested, and re-attach the client to it. I'll kill the 4097 server."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-7121e6826b1949a99841f62e7c7f5e00","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"kill 1968 1959 2>/dev/null; sleep 1; echo \"Server on 4097 stopped\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":35087,"output":686,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":35773,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770915679024}}
